# Massless Charged Particle (standard vector potential) with Lobatto-IIIB-IIIA VPRK Integrators

```julia
run_list(iodeproblem(timestep = Δt, timespan = (0.0, Δt * nt)), :TableauVPRK, tableaus_vprk_lobatto_IIIB_IIIA())
```

## Poincaré Invariants

Relative error of the first and the second Poincaré invariant,

```math
I_{1} = \oint_{\gamma} \vartheta_{i} (q) \, dq^{i}
\qquad \text{and} \qquad
I_{2} = \int_{S} \omega_{ij} (q) \, dq^{i} \wedge dq^{j} ,
```

over a loop and a surface in configuration space advected by each of the methods above — the
problem's own `f_loop` and `f_surface`. The surface lies inside the loop but is not the region the
loop bounds, so the two are different numbers rather than two estimates of one. The time step is
that of the example above; the time interval is much shorter, since one run advects a few hundred
trajectories instead of one.

```julia
run_poincare(iodeproblem(timestep = Δt, timespan = (0.0, Δt * nt_poincare)), :TableauVPRK, tableaus_vprk_lobatto_IIIB_IIIA())
```
